<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuelan M-2 rises 0.19 pct in week to Aug 30.</title>
<headline>Venezuelan M-2 rises 0.19 pct in week to Aug 30.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuelan money supply, as measured by the monetary aggregate M-2, rose 0.19 percent, or eight billion bolivars to 4.296 trillion bolivars in the week to August 30, the central bank said.</p>
<p>At the beginning of 1996, M-2 was 3.530 trillion bolivars.</p>
<p>The monetary base, meanwhile, slipped 0.01 percent, or 200 million bolivars, to 1.077 trillion in the week to Aug 30.</p>
<p>-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2605</p>
